Input: {"correlation_id": "ETH-USDT-1h-1789988399999", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790001000000, "account": {"equity": "9987.374733506756", "available_margin": "9798.812223506756800000000000", "currency": "USDT", "position_mode": "HEDGE", "as_of_ms": 1790001000000}, "position": {"position_id": "wf-main-4", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "side": "LONG", "quantity": "0.345", "mark_price": "2732.79", "ownership_role": "MAIN", "as_of_ms": 1790001000000, "entry_price": "2717.2717", "unrealized_pnl": "5.3538135"}, "positions": [{"position_id": "wf-main-4", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "side": "LONG", "quantity": "0.345", "mark_price": "2732.79", "ownership_role": "MAIN", "as_of_ms": 1790001000000, "entry_price": "2717.2717", "unrealized_pnl": "5.3538135"}], "executor_state": {"as_of_ms": 1790001000000, "controller_id": "brooks-walkforward-10d", "fills_read_status": "available", "executors": [{"executor_id": "wf-exec-7", "status": "RUNNING", "trading_pair": "ETH-USDT", "controller_id": "brooks-walkforward-10d", "position_id": "wf-main-4", "config": {"stop_price": "2702.560000000000000000000000", "target_price": "2745.880000000000000000000001"}}]}, "open_orders": [], "recent_fills": [{"fill_id": "wf-fill-7", "order_id": "wf-fill-7", "position_id": "wf-main-4", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "side": "LONG", "status": "FILLED", "quantity": "0.345", "price": "2717.2717", "fee": "0.37498349460", "filled_at_ms": 1789988699999}], "fills_since_last_event": [], "original_trade_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "ENTER_LONG", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789988399999, "market_context": {"D1": {"regime": "bull-trend breakout", "freshness": "current", "note": "First three consecutive closes above the 2557.46 ceiling (2612.02/2632.98/2642.90) with rising swing lows 2357.18 -> 2358.62 -> 2413.82 -> 2436.87; always-in long."}, "H4": {"regime": "bull channel pressing the 2700.00 range top", "freshness": "current", "note": "Higher lows 2370.54/2436.87/2495.82/2608.83/2568.16; two exact 2700.00 highs (1789804800000, 1789948800000) marked the top, and the M15/H1 spike to 2850.00 has now overshot that level and fallen back to test it."}, "H1": {"note": "Strong bull leg 2568.16 -> 2850.00; last H1 bar (open_time 1789984800000) O 2720.66 H 2721.47 L 2709.56 C 2715.68 is a small inside hesitation bar after the climax H1 bar (open_time 1789981200000, O 2696.51 H 2850.00 L 2694.94 C 2720.66)."}, "M15": {"note": "Climactic spike bar 114 (O 2708.33 H 2850.00 L 2702.56 C 2739.13), then a five-bar tight flag (bars 115-119) holding above the 2700.00 breakout level."}}, "setup": {"type": "bull flag / breakout-pullback long: buy stop above the flag's last bar high with structural stop below the spike bar low", "trigger_status": "pending", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "neutral", "no_trade_reason": null}, "decision_timeframe": "M15", "context_timeframes_used": ["M15", "H1", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "breakout_pullback", "trigger": {"reference": "M15 bar 119 high (last closed bar of the flag; small bull bar closing 2715.68 in the top quarter of its 2709.56-2716.56 range)", "price_field": "high", "price": "2716.56", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 119, "open_time_ms": 1789987500000, "close_time_ms": 1789988399999}, "kind": "stop", "direction": "above"}, "invalidation": {"reference": "M15 bar 114 low (spike bar low, sitting just above the 2700.00 H4/D1 breakout level; a trade below it breaks the pullback low and the whole breakout-pullback)", "price_field": "low", "price": "2702.56", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 114, "open_time_ms": 1789983000000, "close_time_ms": 1789983899999}}, "evidence_for": ["D1 context (current) is a bull-trend breakout: closes 2612.02/2632.98/2642.90 are the first three above the 2557.46 range ceiling, swing lows rise 2357.18 -> 2358.62 -> 2413.82 -> 2436.87, and the M15/H1 rally has now exceeded the D1 spike high 2771 (M15 bar 114 high 2850.00).", "H4 context (current) is an always-in-long bull channel off 2358.62 with higher lows 2370.54, 2436.87, 2495.82, 2608.83, 2568.16; the pullback is holding just above its 2700.00 range top.", "H1 raw bar open_time 1789984800000 (O 2720.66 H 2721.47 L 2709.56 C 2715.68) is an inside hesitation bar, not a bear reversal bar; there is no H1 close below 2694.94, the low of H1 bar open_time 1789981200000, so the H1 trend structure is intact.", "M15 bar 114 (open 2708.33, high 2850.00, low 2702.56, close 2739.13) cleared the 2700.00 range top and the D1 spike high 2771; bars 115-119 then hold above it (lows 2717.36, 2716.28, 2711.92, 2709.60, 2709.56), i.e. a pullback that is holding the breakout zone rather than failing back into the range.", "M15 bars 118 and 119 print an equal-low micro double bottom (2709.60 and 2709.56) with higher closes (2714.49 then 2715.68), and bar 119 closes 2715.68 near its 2716.56 high - a small bull signal bar at the low of the flag.", "Location and trader's equation: stop entry above 2716.56 with invalidation at 2702.56 is about 14.0 points of risk against about 22.6 points to the 2739.13 flag high / spike close, with 2776.28 and 2850.00 beyond, while H1, H4 and D1 are all always-in long."], "evidence_against": ["M15 bar 114 is climactic: range 147.44 points with a 110.87-point upper tail (high 2850.00 versus close 2739.13), far larger than the preceding ~10-point bars, which typically starts a trading range rather than immediate continuation.", "The H1 bar covering 1789981200000-1789984799999 (O 2696.51 H 2850.00 L 2694.94 C 2720.66) closed in the bottom quarter of its range - a climax/possible reversal bar on H1, and the next H1 bar closed lower at 2715.68.", "The pullback has already given back most of the last leg: from the 2850.00 high to the 2709.56 low (bar 119) is about 69% of the 2646.02 -> 2850.00 leg (M15 bar 107 low to bar 114 high), and price at 2715.68 is back in the lower third of the spike bar, below its midpoint 2776.28, with resistance at 2739.13 and 2776.28 before 2850.00.", "Bars 116-119 are a tight, overlapping base (bodies 0.41, 9.15, 2.57 and 1.18 points versus 30.80 on bar 114), so the signal bar is weak; a slip below 2709.56 would put 2700.00/2694.94 back in play before the long can work.", "The H4 read had already flagged 2700.00 as a rejected top (two exact 2700.00 highs), so the 2850.00 spike can also be read as an overshoot/failed breakout now being sold back toward the range ceiling."], "qualitative_confidence": "low", "uncertainty": ["The 2850.00 print is an outlier (147-point bar after a sequence of roughly 4-15 point bars); whether it is genuine liquidity or a data/liquidity artefact cannot be resolved from the supplied bars, and raw bars are treated as authoritative either way.", "Whether the post-climax correction still needs a second leg toward 2700.00/2694.94 before the bull resumes; the five-bar flag is unresolved at the decision time and the pending stop is not yet triggered.", "Signal-bar quality is weak in a tight range after a climax; missing volume, order-flow or indicator data is not treated as a veto or as a reason to abstain."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["A close below 2702.56 (M15 bar 114 low) would break the flag and the breakout-pullback; an additional break of 2694.94 would confirm a failed breakout above 2700.00 and shift the read back to trading range.", "Acceptance above 2739.13 (flag high and spike close) with the following bar holding above it would confirm continuation toward 2776.28 and 2850.00.", "Repeated overlapping closes between 2709.56 and 2739.13 without breaking either edge would mark a new higher trading range and remove the long's edge."]}, "latest_trader_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "ENTER_LONG", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789999199999, "market_context": {"D1": "CONTEXT_ANALYST (current): bull-trend/breakout-spike, always_in long; three consecutive closes above the 2557.46 range ceiling (2612.02/2632.98/2642.90) with higher lows 2357.18-2358.62-2413.82-2436.87; spike high 2771 (bar 89) still overhead.", "H4": "CONTEXT_ANALYST (current): bull-trend/breakout-spike, always_in long; bar 120 (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) is the first close above the twice-tested 2700 high and is a 191.94-point range bar; all 18 closes bars 103-120 hold above 2576.9; 2568.16 (bar 114 low) is the higher-low line of the leg.", "H1": "Bull continuation: bars 117-119 close 2720.00 (open 2715.68), 2734.09 (open 2723.15), 2734.13 (open 2734.08) with rising lows 2713.04/2719.08/2720.15 and rising highs to 2741.55.", "M15": "17-bar tight flag after the 2850 buy-climax spike (bar 102, open 2708.33, high 2850, low 2702.56, close 2739.13); flag low 2709.56 (bar 107), rising lows and rising highs, last bar 119 (open 2724.63, high 2741.55, low 2721.12, close 2734.13) is a bull bar printing a new consolidation high.", "location": "Buying the M15 flag breakout roughly 41 points above the reclaimed H4 2700 breakout level, but below the D1 spike high 2771 and the H4/M15 spike high 2850."}, "setup": {"type": "bull flag / tight-range breakout continuation after higher-timeframe spike", "trigger_status": "pending", "signal_quality": "clear", "location_assessment": "neutral", "no_trade_reason": null}, "decision_timeframe": "M15", "context_timeframes_used": ["H1", "M15", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "breakout", "trigger": {"reference": "M15 bar 119 high (flag breakout level)", "price_field": "high", "price": "2741.55", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 119, "open_time_ms": 1789998300000, "close_time_ms": 1789999199999}, "kind": "stop", "direction": "above"}, "invalidation": {"reference": "M15 bar 107 low (bull-flag low of the post-spike consolidation)", "price_field": "low", "price": "2709.56", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 107, "open_time_ms": 1789987500000, "close_time_ms": 1789988399999}}, "evidence_for": ["M15 bar 119 (open 2724.63, high 2741.55, low 2721.12, close 2734.13) is a bull bar closing in its upper third that fully reverses bar 118 (open 2733.92, close 2721.57) and prints a new high for the consolidation.", "The 17 M15 bars since the 2850 spike (bar 102, open 2708.33, high 2850, low 2702.56, close 2739.13) form a flag with a rising base: lows 2709.56 (bar 107), 2719.08 (bar 113), 2720.15 (bar 118), 2721.12 (bar 119), and rising highs 2727.01 (bar 110) -> 2736.56 (bar 115) -> 2741.55 (bar 119), holding entirely above the H4 2700 breakout level.", "H1 bars 117-119 close 2720.00, 2734.09, 2734.13 with rising lows 2713.04/2719.08/2720.15, so the one-hour timeframe shows the same continuation.", "H4 context (current) bar 120 close 2723.15 is the first close above the twice-tested 2700 resistance; the eight closed M15 bars after that H4 close (opens 1789992000000-1789998300000) all hold between 2719.08 and 2741.55 above 2700, meeting the supplied H4 follow-through transition condition.", "D1 context (current) shows three consecutive closes above the 2557.46 ceiling and an always_in long lean, so higher-timeframe location supports continuation rather than a counter-trend entry."], "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the 2850 spike bar (M15 bar 102) carries a 110.87-point upper tail and closes at 25% of its 147.44-point range - a buy-climax bar - and the entire 17-bar flag sits below its close 2739.13, so the long trigger at 2741.55 is being bought into overhead supply that the market already rejected once.", "The D1 spike high 2771 (context bar 89) is only about 30 points above the 2741.55 trigger, roughly equal to the 32-point distance to the flag-low invalidation, so nearby opposing structure crowds the Trader's Equation.", "The trigger 2741.55 exceeds the prior consolidation high 2739.54 (M15 bar 116) by only about 2 points and no M15 bar has closed above the flag high, so this is a marginal breakout of a tight 32-point range rather than a decisive one.", "Higher-timeframe precedent is failure-prone: earlier upside spikes (D1 bars 110 and 113; H4 bars 61 and 81) were rejected and retraced, and H4 bar 120's 126.85-point tail shows the 2850 high was sold."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["The trigger is pending: 2741.55 has not traded and the last close 2734.13 is still inside the flag, so the breakout is not yet confirmed.", "Closed bars do not yet show whether the flag resolves as trend resumption or as a lower high against the 2850 buy-climax spike.", "The current H4 bar has not closed, so H4 acceptance of the 2700/2850 breakout remains unverified.", "D1 context is one bar behind intraday price (last D1 close 2642.90 versus M15 close 2734.13), so the 2771 resistance may be stale relative to the current spike."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["An M15 close back below the flag low 2709.56 negates the bull flag and shifts the read to failed breakout / return into range, removing the long case.", "An M15 close below the spike bar low 2702.56 or the H4 breakout level 2700 would break the H4 breakout and shift the read toward a trading range below 2700.", "Decisive M15 closes above 2741.55 and then above the D1 spike high 2771 would confirm continuation toward the 2850 spike high.", "Continued overlap between 2709.56 and 2741.55 without a close above 2741.55 would turn the flag into a range at the highs and argue for NO_TRADE until a clearer breakout or pullback appears."]}, "latest_market_context": {"schema": "brooks.market-context.v1", "role": "HTF_ANALYST", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789948799999, "timeframe": "D1", "observations": ["Window opens at 2116.86 and falls to 1368.42 (bar 13 low, close 1568.55), then reverses; final close 2642.90 is about +24.9% versus the first open and about +93% above the window low.", "Bars 87-89 are the spike: 1916.51 to 2252.16, 2252.20 to 2326.32, 2326.31 to 2515.30, with the window high 2771 printed on bar 89.", "Bars 90-116 are two-sided: overlapping bodies, highs at 2557.46 (bar 95) and 2609.02 (bar 113), lows clustered 2357.18-2425.44; bar 110 spiked to 2680 and closed 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 117-119 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 \u2014 the first consecutive closes above the 2557.46 ceiling; bar 117 has open 2446.22, high 2643.52, low 2436.87, range 206.65, closing in its top quarter; bar 118 reaches 2700.", "Bar 119 (open 2632.98, high 2645.88, low 2568.16, close 2642.90) is a 77.72-range bar closing near its high while holding above the range ceiling; it makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700).", "Recent lows rise: 2357.18 (bar 101), 2358.62 (bar 114), 2370.54 (bar 115), 2413.82 (bar 116), 2436.87 (bar 117), 2568.16 (bar 119).", "Price 2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the post-spike section is not yet a confirmed new-high trend."], "evidence_against": ["The breakout is only three bars; the preceding 27 bars overlap heavily and the region 2357-2557 can still be read as the operating trading range rather than broken.", "Two earlier upside probes failed to hold: bar 110 high 2680 closed 2514.72, bar 113 high 2609.02 closed 2514.07, so upside spikes in this region have recently been rejected.", "2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the whole post-spike section can be read as one broad trading range whose upper extreme has not been exceeded.", "Bar 119 makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700) with a lower tail to 2568.16, a pause rather than a strong continuation bar, and bar 114 had just traded down to 2358.62 four bars before the breakout."], "uncertainty": ["V2 D1 context adapted for the V1 PM input."]}, "management_history": [{"schema": "brooks.management-decision.v2", "role": "POSITION_MANAGER", "decision_time_ms": 1789988760142, "action": "HOLD", "position_ids": ["wf-main-4"], "reason": "The single MAIN long is coherent with its fill and executor state, margin is SAFE, no hedge leg exists, and the documented breakout-pull